# One line: the public Hoody gateway URL (https).
# It is your computer's terminal URL with `terminal-1` replaced by
# `http-8765`, e.g.:
#   https://<project-id>-<computer-id>-http-8765.<server>.computers.hoody.com
# Written by: ./setup-muse.sh --hoody <url>
# The URL is public by default — the Bearer token in gateway-token.txt
# is what guards the gateway. Set proxy permissions on your Hoody
# project if you want the URL itself locked down.
https://<project-id>-<computer-id>-http-8765.<server>.computers.hoody.com
